*=======================================================================================
* opamp_rtr_params.spice
* Seed / frozen design parameters for opamp_rtr.spice (PyOPUS designpar mirror)
*
* NOT included by opamp_rtr.spice during PyOPUS optimization (see note there).
* Standalone use: .include this file BEFORE opamp_rtr.spice in a manual deck.
* After optimization: paste the optimized values here to freeze the design.
*
* Values below are the winner of the 40-corner optimize_full_corner run
* (compute_results/optimize_full_corner.sqlite): gain 41.3 dB, ugbw 1.55 MHz,
* pm 71.0 deg, idd 327 uA, tracking error 1.1 mV, noise 25.4 uV, thd 4.3e-4,
* all worst-case over ff/fs/sf/ss/tt x 8 sub-corners.
* The four v_bias_*/v_ref_* voltages of that run are replaced here by the
* current-mode bias generator (w_bias_*/w_ref_*/i_ref) - see opamp_rtr.spice.
*=======================================================================================
* PMOS input pair
.param w_diff_p=6.5e-6
.param l_diff_p=2.93e-6
* NMOS input pair
.param w_diff_n=1.65e-5
.param l_diff_n=3.5e-6
* Input tails
.param w_tail_p=2.1e-5
.param w_tail_n=7.6e-6
* Shared L of every current-source / mirror device (bias generator included):
* the mirror ratios are pure width ratios only because L is common
.param l_bias=3.6e-6
* NMOS mirror load
.param w_load_n=4.12e-5
.param l_load_n=9.7e-6
* PMOS mirror load
.param w_load_p=1.94e-6
.param l_load_p=1.9e-6
* Output PMOS (was pinned at its 150u upper bound in the winning run)
.param w_out_p=1.2e-4
.param l_out_p=5.65e-7
* Output NMOS
.param w_out_n=7.97e-5
.param l_out_n=1.9e-6
* Monticelli floating NMOS + N-stack diodes
.param w_ab_n=3.47e-5
.param l_ab_n=2.55e-6
* Monticelli floating PMOS + P-stack diodes
.param w_ab_p=3.93e-6
.param l_ab_p=4.54e-6
* I_ab feed (PMOS XM15/XM17/XM23) and sink (NMOS XM16/XM20/XM24)
.param w_ab_src=1.47e-6
.param w_ab_snk=6.85e-7
* Miller caps
.param c_miller_p=3e-13
.param c_miller_n=3.3e-13
* Constant-gm current switches
.param w_sw_p=5.87e-5
.param w_sw_n=1e-5
* gm-switch mirrors: diode (1) and output (2) devices; ratio w2/w1 sets how much
* the surviving pair is boosted (1x for weak inversion .. 3x for strong)
.param w_gmn1=4.1e-6
.param w_gmn2=1.45e-5
.param w_gmp1=8.5e-7
.param w_gmp2=1.1e-6
*=======================================================================================
* Current-mode bias generator (replaces the four distributed bias voltages).
* External reference current into the ibias pin; every branch of the generator
* carries i_ref, and each biased device mirrors it by W ratio at l_bias.
.param i_ref=5.3e-7
* NMOS master diode XB1 + mirror legs XB2/XB6. I_tail_n = i_ref*w_tail_n/w_bias_n,
* so w_bias_n = w_tail_n/2 seeds the NMOS tail at 2*i_ref.
.param w_bias_n=3.46e-6
* PMOS master diode XB3 + mirror leg XB4. Same 1:2 seed for the PMOS side.
.param w_bias_p=9.87e-5
* Constant-gm reference diodes XB5 (low) / XB7 (high). NARROWER than the master
* diodes at the same current => higher |Vgs| => the switch reference sits further
* from its rail, which is where the crossover has to be.
.param w_ref_n=2.81e-5
.param w_ref_p=1.12e-5
